{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation complete — pushed as Gerrit change 1796 (Change-Id I42e35c80dac3feac7701ae56f696fb59fdf1f1c5, commit 0f18955862), awaiting LLM-Review + Verified votes. Not submitted; ticket stays in_progress.\n\nWORKSTREAM A — budget recalibration (withheld-oracle TDD, RED verified first):\n- verify_step_floor(criteria_count, verify_cfg, direct_children=0) = clamp(24*c + 16*direct_children + 16, 160, 960); _VERIFY_STEP_FLOOR_MAX 480->960; defaults 8->24 steps/criterion, 48->160 floor-min. New typed config keys completion_verify_child_traversal_steps / completion_verify_fixed_overhead_steps (both 16) in _config_schema.py + validators in _config_sections.py.\n- Both consumers wired: primary sizing (completion.py, child enumeration via shared fail-open helper — never raises, fails open to childless floor) and plan_recovery_pool (direct_children pass-through, forwarded by sole caller _run_successors). Docstring oracle + hard pins in tests/unit/workflow/test_completion_banking.py updated (childless c=8 floor 208/N 104/global 156/successor 52; childful c=8,k=4 floor 272; clamp c=60 -> 960/480/720/240).\n- Contract pins rewritten in tests/interfaces/contracts/test_completion_budget.py: floor(1)=160, (8)=208, (40)=(100)=960; new tests: child-traversal term, epic-request floors, childful>childless at equal criteria, enumeration-failure fail-open.\n\nWORKSTREAM B — cross-run PASS-verdict cache (new module src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_verdict_cache.py, 291 LOC):\n- Persist ONLY validated PASS at finalize (after _validate_coverage, before return; atomic tmp+os.replace; bank-backed records only; insufficiency/FAIL never written) at .rebar/cache/completion_verdicts/<ticket>/<criterion-hash>.json. Repo root resolves via _config_sources.repo_root (REBAR_ROOT > git toplevel), never bare cwd.\n- Scoped content fingerprint (net-new): git blob SHAs of file_impact paths (batched rev-parse, per-path fallback), absent path -> sentinel, git failure -> None (reuse disabled, fail-open to re-verification); empty impact + children -> union of DIRECT-child impact blobs; childless+empty -> whole-tree sha; childful with zero impact surface -> None.\n- Seeding at run start via _primary_manifest_contract(bank): valid entries seed the run bank stamped seeded:true; primary_criteria_manifest gains seeded_ids and omits them; an \"already credited — do not re-verify\" directive block is appended to the primary context.\n- merge_finalizer_with_bank: seeded records bypass finalizer judgment (echo incl. met:false downgrade replaced by the bank record; omission appended; a contradicted finalizer-global FAIL recomputes to PASS when all records met). Same-run downgrade preservation regression-tested — rule keys strictly on the seeded flag.\n- Module-size pressure: _banked_evidence_payload moved recovery->banking along its call-graph seam (re-exported; test import path preserved). completion.py 799, completion_recovery.py 795, banking 700 — all under the 800 cap.\n\nTESTS: tests/unit/workflow/test_completion_verdict_cache.py (18 tests: fingerprint x6, persist x2, load/invalidation x3, seeding/manifest/directive x3, merge both directions x2, bank concurrent-close isolation, runaway backstop under 960). All RED-first (module absent / pins failing), now green. Full runs: tests/unit/workflow 721 passed (5 pre-existing environmental failures in test_bridge_provider_wrappers_heldout.py — host git safe.bareRepository config, untouched by this change); tests/interfaces/contracts 206 passed; tests/unit -k \"completion or budget\" 356 passed.\n\nMUTATION PASS (manual, scoped to changed functions; mutmut present but needs pyproject [tool.mutmut] config = repo mutation, so scoped manual pass used): 11 mutants, 11 killed (M1 drop child term, M2 clamp stays 480, M3 drop overhead, M4 pool drops direct_children forwarding, M5 fingerprint always tree-fallback, M6 persist PASS-only inverted, M7 seeded bypass inverted, M8 manifest omission inverted, M9 load drops fingerprint check, M10 seed omits seeded stamp, M11 enumeration fail-open inverted). Kill rate 11/11 = 100%.\n\nGATES: make lint clean, make typecheck clean (542 files), complexity ratchet new=0 increased=0, runaway guards untouched (test_agent_call_runaway_guard_c827 green + new backstop test at max_iterations=960)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786749498429501001,"uuid":"ad629b7b-3ed7-4f98-99cb-37d023f0620f"}